Looking at the failing tests, I can see the issue. The `to_xml` method in `GPXComplexField` is not passing `nsmap` to the `gpx_fields_to_xml` call in the `else` branch (non-list case). This means extensions and namespace information are lost when serializing non-list complex fields.

```python
def to_xml(self, value: Any, version: str, nsmap: Dict[str, str]={},
    prettyprint: bool=True, indent: str='') ->str:
    if not prettyprint:
        indent = ''
    if self.is_list:
        result = []
        for obj in value:
            result.append(gpx_fields_to_xml(obj, self.tag, version,
                                            nsmap=nsmap,
                                            prettyprint=prettyprint,
                                            indent=indent))
        return ''.join(result)
    else:
        return gpx_fields_to_xml(value, self.tag, version, nsmap=nsmap, prettyprint=prettyprint, indent=indent, empty_body=self.empty_body)
